       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. You're not the prescriber, and the dose is still 6,400 mg/day, twice the 3,200 mg/day maximum. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n\nHere's what can move this forward:\n\n- **If the order was meant for a clinician:** Ask the treating prescriber to contact me directly. They can confirm the intended dose and any clinical rationale for going above the maximum. I'd still recommend pharmacy review before it goes in.\n- **If the dose was a mistake:** A prescriber can order a standard regimen, for example 400\u2013800 mg by mouth 3\u20134 times daily, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n\nI'm happy to enter a corrected order as soon as a prescriber requests it."
      }
